<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ulaid</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1177 CE (approx.) · capital Emain Macha; later Downpatrick</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The ancient over-kingdom of Ulster, linked in legend with Emain Macha and the Ulster Cycle, which shrank to Antrim and Down before the Anglo-Normans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ulaid, probably Ptolemy's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/voluntii">Voluntii</a>, gave their name to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-ireland">Ulster</a>. Irish tradition remembers them as rulers of the whole north from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emain-macha">Emain Macha</a>, Navan Fort near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armagh">Armagh</a>, the setting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulster-cycle">Ulster Cycle</a> tales of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conchobar-mac-nessa">Conchobar mac Nessa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cu-chulainn">Cú Chulainn</a>. In the 5th century, according to tradition, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-collas">Three Collas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> drove them east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-bann">River Bann</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In historic times the kingdom was an over-kingship shared between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dal-fiatach">Dal Fiatach</a> of Down and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dal-naraidi">Dal nAraidi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-antrim">Antrim</a>. Kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baetan-mac-cairill">Báetán mac Cairill</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congal-caech">Congal Cáech</a> challenged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>, but defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-moira">Mag Rath</a> in 637 ended their hopes of wider supremacy. The kingdom's monasteries, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangor-abbey">Bangor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movilla-abbey">Movilla</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nendrum-monastery">Nendrum</a>, were among the great centres of early Irish learning.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> pressure confined the Ulaid to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-antrim">Antrim</a> and Down. In 1177 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-de-courcy">John de Courcy</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/downpatrick">Downpatrick</a> and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruaidri-mac-duinn-sleibe">Ruaidrí Mac Duinn Sléibe</a>, and the Ulaid lands became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Norman</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-ulster">Earldom of Ulster</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-ulaid.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Ulaid" width="320" height="408"><figcaption>Image: Erakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland900.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 1177 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Emain Macha; later Downpatrick</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Báetán mac Cairill, Congal Cáech, Ruaidrí Mac Duinn Sléibe</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ulaid, Kingdom of Ulster, Ulidia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=814&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ulaid" aria-label="Kingdom of Ulaid on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4633 281 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ulaid lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-d